  <div class="tool-head"><span>Appraisal prep scorecard</span><i>12 questions · about two minutes</i></div>
  <div class="tool-body">
    <div class="tool-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get written confirmation that coverage is accepted. If the claim was denied outright, talk to a Kansas attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask in writing for the full line-item estimate, not just the payment summary."><span>Do you have the carrier’s complete, itemized estimate?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get an independent line-item estimate. A one-line bid won’t hold up in front of a panel."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo and note the date each was taken. Add photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the storm or event?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Look in the Conditions section for the paragraph titled ‘Appraisal’ and note any deadlines."><span>Have you found and read the appraisal clause in your policy?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the clause and put the date on your calendar. The claim timeline builder can help."><span>Do you know the deadline in your policy’s ‘Suit Against Us’ clause?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Finish reasonable temporary repairs, such as tarps, and keep every receipt."><span>Have temporary repairs been made, with receipts saved?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Download it from your insurer’s portal or ask your agent."><span>Do you have your current declarations page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure wet insulation, decking and interior cavities are inspected so the scope is complete."><span>Has hidden damage (decking, attic, wall cavities) been checked?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Gather letters, emails and claim notes in date order."><span>Is your correspondence with the insurer organized by date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run your numbers in the appraisal payoff projector. A small gap may not justify fees."><span>Is the gap between estimates more than about 10% or $5,000?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Return any requested proof of loss before the deadline in the request."><span>If a sworn proof of loss was requested, has it been sent on time?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn ghost small" data-reset>Reset answers</button></div>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-out" aria-live="polite" style="grid-template-columns:minmax(220px,300px) 1fr;align-items:start">
      <div>
        <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#e3e9f5" stroke-width="18"/><path data-o="arc" d="M20 100 A80 80 0 0 1 180 100" fill="none" stroke="#f1ad02" stroke-width="18" stroke-dasharray="251.3" stroke-dashoffset="251.3" style="transition:stroke-dashoffset .5s,stroke .3s"/></svg>
        <div class="gauge-num"><span data-o="score">–</span></div>
        <p class="hint" style="text-align:center">Answered <span data-o="count">0 / 12</span></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="out-msg" data-o="verdict"></p>
        <p class="todo-h">Your to-do list</p>
        <ul data-o="todo" style="margin:0;padding-left:1.1em"></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div>
<p class="hint tool-note">For planning only. Results depend on the figures you enter and your policy’s terms. They are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<h2>How the score is weighted</h2>
<p>Coverage, estimates and evidence carry the most weight because they decide whether appraisal is the right tool and how well your number will hold up. Paperwork matters too, but it is easier to fix.</p>
<h2>Reading your score</h2>
<ul><li><strong>75 and up:</strong> a solid file. A professional review of the gap is the logical next step.</li>
<li><strong>45 to 74:</strong> close the open items first; each one strengthens your position.</li>
<li><strong>Under 45:</strong> demanding appraisal now could lock in a low number. Build the file first.</li></ul>

<h2>Questions about this calculator</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary><span>Is anything saved or sent?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>No. The scorecard runs entirely in your browser and nothing is stored.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>Can I share my result?</span><svg class="pl" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. Take a screenshot of your to-do list and bring it to a consultation.</p></div></details></div>
